  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1228 AM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nA large upper level ridge will remain centered near the Four Corners \nregion through Monday, resulting in a continuation of the hot and \ndry conditions that we have seen over the last several days. Since \nthe ridge will be centered well to our west, highs are forecast to \nbe near seasonal normals. Highs will be in the mid 90s to near 100. \nOvernight lows will generally be in the low to mid 70s. \n\nTuesday into the middle part of next week, the aforementioned upper \nlevel ridge will begin to shift east, toward Texas. This will result \nin a slight increase in temperatures Tuesday and Wednesday with \nhighs in the mid 90s to near 103.",
